{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The search results confirm that `ADR-0004` and `KI_rich_syntax.md` (for `Table`) and `KI_rich_null.md` (for ratio solvers) are the most relevant. I'll start by reading `ADR-0004` to understand the decisions behind ratio distribution."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_lstmwiFbaavOQFvEas4H","name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","arguments":{"rel_path":".ki-base/decisions/0004-ratio-distribution-and-layout.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"google/gemini-2.5-flash","usage":{"input":808,"output":116,"cacheRead":5770,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":6694,"cost":{"input":0.00024239999999999998,"output":0.00029,"cacheRead":0.00017309999999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0007055,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794170975180,"responseId":"gen-1794170975-quKBw279qq8zPU3MWLF9","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":996,"thinkingLevel":"off"}}
{"type":"tool_execution_start","toolCallId":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_lstmwiFbaavOQFvEas4H","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","args":{"rel_path":".ki-base/decisions/0004-ratio-distribution-and-layout.md"}}
{"type":"tool_execution_end","toolCallId":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_lstmwiFbaavOQFvEas4H","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0004: Ratio Distribution & Column Allocation\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nWhen rendering tables and multi-pane split layouts, columns and panels have competing size constraints: minimum width, maximum width, fixed cell counts, or proportional ratios (`ratio=1`, `ratio=2`). In collapsed views or deeply nested tables, total available space can shrink to zero or negative values, risking `ZeroDivisionError` or layout breakage.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Two-Pass Space Resolution (`rich/_ratio.py`):**  \n   Space allocation via `ratio_resolve(total: int, edges: Sequence[Edge]) -> List[int]` must strictly adhere to the two-pass algorithm:\n   - **Pass 1 (Fixed & Minimum Constraints):** Allocate absolute minimum widths and fixed sizes first. Subtract allocated space from `total`.\n   - **Pass 2 (Proportional Ratios):** Distribute remaining space among flexible edges according to their `ratio` weights.\n2. **Boundary & Zero Protection Invariants:**\n   - If remaining space is zero or negative, flexible edges must receive `edge.minimum_size` (or 0) without performing division by total ratio weights.\n   - Algorithms must never raise `ZeroDivisionError` on zero-weight column sets; instead, distribute space evenly or fall back to minimum sizes.\n3. **Integer Conservation:**\n   - The sum of resolved column widths must never exceed `total` space allocated by the parent container. Fractional remainders are distributed deterministically across flexible columns.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Prevents crashes in nested or collapsed table views under narrow terminal dimensions.\n- Decouples table column layout logic from split-pane `Layout` mathematics.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"structuredContent":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0004: Ratio Distribution & Column Allocation\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nWhen rendering tables and multi-pane split layouts, columns and panels have competing size constraints: minimum width, maximum width, fixed cell counts, or proportional ratios (`ratio=1`, `ratio=2`). In collapsed views or deeply nested tables, total available space can shrink to zero or negative values, risking `ZeroDivisionError` or layout breakage.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Two-Pass Space Resolution (`rich/_ratio.py`):**  \n   Space allocation via `ratio_resolve(total: int, edges: Sequence[Edge]) -> List[int]` must strictly adhere to the two-pass algorithm:\n   - **Pass 1 (Fixed & Minimum Constraints):** Allocate absolute minimum widths and fixed sizes first. Subtract allocated space from `total`.\n   - **Pass 2 (Proportional Ratios):** Distribute remaining space among flexible edges according to their `ratio` weights.\n2. **Boundary & Zero Protection Invariants:**\n   - If remaining space is zero or negative, flexible edges must receive `edge.minimum_size` (or 0) without performing division by total ratio weights.\n   - Algorithms must never raise `ZeroDivisionError` on zero-weight column sets; instead, distribute space evenly or fall back to minimum sizes.\n3. **Integer Conservation:**\n   - The sum of resolved column widths must never exceed `total` space allocated by the parent container. Fractional remainders are distributed deterministically across flexible columns.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Prevents crashes in nested or collapsed table views under narrow terminal dimensions.\n- Decouples table column layout logic from split-pane `Layout` mathematics.\n"}]}},"isError":false,"durationMs":32}
{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_lstmwiFbaavOQFvEas4H","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0004: Ratio Distribution & Column Allocation\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nWhen rendering tables and multi-pane split layouts, columns and panels have competing size constraints: minimum width, maximum width, fixed cell counts, or proportional ratios (`ratio=1`, `ratio=2`). In collapsed views or deeply nested tables, total available space can shrink to zero or negative values, risking `ZeroDivisionError` or layout breakage.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Two-Pass Space Resolution (`rich/_ratio.py`):**  \n   Space allocation via `ratio_resolve(total: int, edges: Sequence[Edge]) -> List[int]` must strictly adhere to the two-pass algorithm:\n   - **Pass 1 (Fixed & Minimum Constraints):** Allocate absolute minimum widths and fixed sizes first. Subtract allocated space from `total`.\n   - **Pass 2 (Proportional Ratios):** Distribute remaining space among flexible edges according to their `ratio` weights.\n2. **Boundary & Zero Protection Invariants:**\n   - If remaining space is zero or negative, flexible edges must receive `edge.minimum_size` (or 0) without performing division by total ratio weights.\n   - Algorithms must never raise `ZeroDivisionError` on zero-weight column sets; instead, distribute space evenly or fall back to minimum sizes.\n3. **Integer Conservation:**\n   - The sum of resolved column widths must never exceed `total` space allocated by the parent container. Fractional remainders are distributed deterministically across flexible columns.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Prevents crashes in nested or collapsed table views under narrow terminal dimensions.\n- Decouples table column layout logic from split-pane `Layout` mathematics.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":32,"timestamp":1794170976214}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_lstmwiFbaavOQFvEas4H","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0004: Ratio Distribution & Column Allocation\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nWhen rendering tables and multi-pane split layouts, columns and panels have competing size constraints: minimum width, maximum width, fixed cell counts, or proportional ratios (`ratio=1`, `ratio=2`). In collapsed views or deeply nested tables, total available space can shrink to zero or negative values, risking `ZeroDivisionError` or layout breakage.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Two-Pass Space Resolution (`rich/_ratio.py`):**  \n   Space allocation via `ratio_resolve(total: int, edges: Sequence[Edge]) -> List[int]` must strictly adhere to the two-pass algorithm:\n   - **Pass 1 (Fixed & Minimum Constraints):** Allocate absolute minimum widths and fixed sizes first. Subtract allocated space from `total`.\n   - **Pass 2 (Proportional Ratios):** Distribute remaining space among flexible edges according to their `ratio` weights.\n2. **Boundary & Zero Protection Invariants:**\n   - If remaining space is zero or negative, flexible edges must receive `edge.minimum_size` (or 0) without performing division by total ratio weights.\n   - Algorithms must never raise `ZeroDivisionError` on zero-weight column sets; instead, distribute space evenly or fall back to minimum sizes.\n3. **Integer Conservation:**\n   - The sum of resolved column widths must never exceed `total` space allocated by the parent container. Fractional remainders are distributed deterministically across flexible columns.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Prevents crashes in nested or collapsed table views under narrow terminal dimensions.\n- Decouples table column layout logic from split-pane `Layout` mathematics.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":32,"timestamp":1794170976214}}
