t directory)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of entries to return (default: 500)"}}}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_instructions","description":"Get workflow instructions and project rules for ki-manager. Available documents:\n- 'overview' — global AI rules and project navigation\n- 'knowledge-items' — table of registered KI files\n- 'create-adr' — workflow: document architectural decisions\n- 'expand-knowledge' — workflow: deep enrichment of KI files\n- 'scaffold-knowledge' — workflow: bulk scaffold of uncovered modules\n- 'sync-knowledge' — workflow: sync KI after code changes\nCall this before starting any documentation workflow task.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"document":{"type":"string","description":"Document name from the list above (e.g. 'create-adr')"}},"required":["document"]}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_list","description":"List Knowledge Items (KI) and Architecture Decision Records (ADRs) registered in the active project. Provides a structured overview of all documented modules, topics, and architectural decisions.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"scope":{"type":"string","enum":["all","ki","adr"],"default":"all","description":"Filter by document type: 'all' (default), 'ki' (Knowledge Items), or 'adr' (Architecture Decision Records)."},"format":{"type":"string","enum":["markdown","json"],"default":"markdown","description":"Output format: 'markdown' (structured tables, default) or 'json'."},"filter":{"type":"string","description":"Optional substring to filter by filename, title, summary, or covered module."}}}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_search","description":"Search Knowledge Items (KI) and ADRs by keywords using BM25 ranking (pure Python). Returns matching paths, titles, relevance scores, and text snippets. Use this tool to find relevant documentation without full codebase scans.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string","description":"Search query keywords (e.g. 'workspace detection' or 'dependency management')."},"scope":{"type":"string","enum":["all","ki","adr"],"default":"all","description":"Scope of search: 'all' (default), 'ki' (knowledge items), or 'adr' (architecture decision records)."},"limit":{"type":"integer","default":5,"description":"Maximum number of results to return (default: 5)."},"offset":{"type":"integer","default":0,"description":"Result offset for pagination (default: 0)."},"page":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"default":1,"description":"Page number for pagination (1-based, alternative to offset)."},"format":{"type":"string","enum":["markdown","json"],"default":"markdown","description":"Output format: 'markdown' (compact list, default) or 'json'."}},"required":["query"]}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","description":"Read a Knowledge Item (KI) or ADR markdown file. Supports optional section filtering (by markdown header), character limits, and offset.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"rel_path":{"type":"string","description":"Path or filename of the Knowledge Item or ADR (e.g. 'KI_architecture.md', 'knowledge/KI_architecture.md', or '001_some.md')."},"section":{"type":"string","description":"Optional markdown section title to extract (e.g. 'Architecture' or 'Known Issues')."},"max_chars":{"type":"integer","description":"Optional maximum number of characters to return (truncates if exceeded)."},"offset":{"type":"integer","default":0,"description":"Optional character offset to start reading from (default: 0)."}},"required":["rel_path"]}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_tools","description":"Inspect available ki-manager tools and their schemas. Call without arguments to list all tools grouped by category. Provide 'name' to inspect the exact inputSchema of a specific tool before calling it via ki_call or ki_mutate.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"Optional tool name to get full JSON schema (e.g. 'audit_coverage')."},"group":{"type":"string","description":"Optional category group filter (init_registry, coverage_analysis, scaffold, config_adr, files, git_state)."}}}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_call","description":"Execute a read-only ki-manager tool. Available tools: analyze_all_dependencies, analyze_dependencies, analyze_module, audit_coverage, check_ki_drift, find_unmapped_files, generate_dir_index, git_diff_secured, ki_graph_visualize, ki_list_projects, ki_scaffold_status, ki_split_analyze, ki_status, read_know_file. Use ki_tools(name=...) to check arguments. For mutating operations, use ki_mutate.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"tool":{"type":"string","description":"Name of the read-only tool to call.","enum":["analyze_all_dependencies","analyze_dependencies","analyze_module","audit_coverage","check_ki_drift","find_unmapped_files","generate_dir_index","git_diff_secured","ki_graph_visualize","ki_list_projects","ki_scaffold_status","ki_split_analyze","ki_status","read_know_file"]},"args":{"type":"object","description":"Arguments dictionary to pass to the tool.","default":{}}},"required":["tool"]}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_mutate","description":"Execute a state-modifying ki-manager tool. Available tools: add_ki_to_config, create_adr, edit_doc_config, edit_know_file, git_checkpoint, git_restore, ki_finalize_scaffolds, ki_init_project, ki_migrate_project, ki_prune_registry, ki_register_project, ki_scaffold, ki_split, make_know_dir, restore_mapping, save_state, sync_agents_md, update_last_verified, write_know_file. Use ki_tools(name=...) to check arguments.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"tool":{"type":"string","description":"Name of the mutating tool to call.","enum":["add_ki_to_config","create_adr","edit_doc_config","edit_know_file","git_checkpoint","git_restore","ki_finalize_scaffolds","ki_init_project","ki_migrate_project","ki_prune_registry","ki_register_project","ki_scaffold","ki_split","make_know_dir","restore_mapping","save_state","sync_agents_md","update_last_verified","write_know_file"]},"args":{"type":"object","description":"Arguments dictionary to pass to the tool.","default":{}}},"required":["tool"]}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Bugfix: Table Ratio Calculation and Flexible Column Collapse\n\nProblem Description:\nWhen rendering tables with a mix of fixed-width columns and flexible ratio columns in constrained console widths (e.g. nested tables, or dashboards with Console(width=60) and expand=True), flexible ratio columns collapse to zero width, producing collapsed borders '||' with completely vanished column headers and cell values. \n\nAdditionally, rendering empty tables with expand=True in constrained widths or with zero ratios crashes with unhandled AssertionErrors (\"Sum of ratios must be > 0\") or ZeroDivisionErrors during ratio calculation.\n\nReproduction:\n```python\nconsole = Console(width=60, record=True)\ntable = Table(title=\"Worker Dashboard\", expand=True)\ntable.add_column(\"Service\", width=22)\ntable.add_column(\"Host\", width=18)\ntable.add_column(\"Load\", ratio=1)\ntable.add_row(\"Database Primary\", \"db-node-01.internal\", \"82%\")\n\nconsole.print(table)\nrendered = console.export_text()\n# Bug: 'Load' header and '82%' cell vanish completely into collapsed borders '||'\n```\n\nRequirements:\n1. Flexible ratio columns must maintain a viable minimum width (at least 1 character for content plus column padding) rather than collapsing to invisible 0-width columns with vanished headers and data.\n2. Ratio calculations and space distributions must gracefully handle edge cases (zero available space, negative remaining space, or all-zero ratios) without crashing with unhandled AssertionErrors or ZeroDivisionErrors.\n3. Existing unit tests must continue to pass without regressions."}],"timestamp":1794170973664},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Okay, I understand the problem. The core issue is that flexible ratio columns in `rich.table.Table` can collapse to zero width, making their content disappear, and that edge cases in ratio calculation can lead to crashes.\n\nI need to investigate the `rich.table` and `rich._ratio` modules to address these issues. I will start by searching for relevant Knowledge Items to guide my investigation, focusing on table layout and ratio distribution."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_search_gQSQwzSBSPD12IuhAdSj","name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_search","arguments":{"query":"table layout ratio distribution column collapse","scope":"ki"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"google/gemini-2.5-flash","usage":{"input":84,"output":123,"cacheRead":5735,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":5942,"cost":{"input":0.0000252,"output":0.00030750000000000005,"cacheRead":0.00017204999999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00050475,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794170973717,"responseId":"gen-1794170973-FfTaDOkv8mEQKzxawq0J","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":1364,"thinkingLevel":"off"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_search_gQSQwzSBSPD12IuhAdSj","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 14 result(s) for \"table layout ratio distribution column collapse\" [Page 1/3 (showing 1-5)]:\n\n> 💡 **Next page**: `ki_search(query=\"table layout ratio distribution column collapse\", page=2)` (or `offset=5`)\n\n1. [KI] **ADR-0004: Ratio Distribution & Column Allocation** (`.ki-base/decisions/0004-ratio-distribution-and-layout.md`, score: 11.241)\n   > # ADR-0004: Ratio Distribution & Column Allocation - **Status:** Accepted - **Date:** 2026-11-08 - **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers ## Context When...\n2. [KI] **KI: Rich Core (Syntax, Tables, Text & Tracebacks)** (`.ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_syntax.md`, score: 6.994)\n   > <!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 --> # KI: Rich Core (Syntax, Tables, Text & Tracebacks) ## Overview Implements high-level data presentation components: `Table` (grid formatting with auto-wrapping), `Text` (styled...\n3. [KI] **KI: Rich Core (Internal Utilities & Platform Adaptors)** (`.ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_null.md`, score: 5.84)\n   > ...Overview Provides internal mathematical routines, layout ratio solvers, text wrapping primitives, platform Win32 console structures, and base ABC protocols. It forms the low-level foundation for rendering...\n4. [KI] **KI: Rich Core (Layouts, Highlighters & Logging)** (`.ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_default.md`, score: 5.1)\n   > <!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 --> # KI: Rich Core (Layouts, Highlighters & Logging) ## Overview Houses split-screen terminal layout panes (`Layout`), pattern regex highlighters (`Highlighter`), JSON syntax...\n5. [KI] **KI: Rich Core (Console, Alignment & Core Layouts)** (`.ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_align.md`, score: 3.78)\n   > ...2026-11-08 --> # KI: Rich Core (Console, Alignment & Core Layouts) ## Overview Central pipeline of Rich: houses the primary `Console` class, ANSI escape sequence decoder, cell width calculators, border box constants,...\n\n*Showing 5 of 14 results. Call `ki_search(query='table layout ratio distribution column collapse', page=2)` (or `offset=5`) to view more.*"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_search"},"isError":false,"durationMs":82,"timestamp":1794170975171},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The search results confirm that `ADR-0004` and `KI_rich_syntax.md` (for `Table`) and `KI_rich_null.md` (for ratio solvers) are the most relevant. I'll start by reading `ADR-0004` to understand the decisions behind ratio distribution."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_lstmwiFbaavOQFvEas4H","name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","arguments":{"rel_path":".ki-base/decisions/0004-ratio-distribution-and-layout.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"google/gemini-2.5-flash","usage":{"input":808,"output":116,"cacheRead":5770,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":6694,"cost":{"input":0.00024239999999999998,"output":0.00029,"cacheRead":0.00017309999999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0007055,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794170975180,"responseId":"gen-1794170975-quKBw279qq8zPU3MWLF9","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":996,"thinkingLevel":"off"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_lstmwiFbaavOQFvEas4H","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0004: Ratio Distribution & Column Allocation\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nWhen rendering tables and multi-pane split layouts, columns and panels have competing size constraints: minimum width, maximum width, fixed cell counts, or proportional ratios (`ratio=1`, `ratio=2`). In collapsed views or deeply nested tables, total available space can shrink to zero or negative values, risking `ZeroDivisionError` or layout breakage.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Two-Pass Space Resolution (`rich/_ratio.py`):**  \n   Space allocation via `ratio_resolve(total: int, edges: Sequence[Edge]) -> List[int]` must strictly adhere to the two-pass algorithm:\n   - **Pass 1 (Fixed & Minimum Constraints):** Allocate absolute minimum widths and fixed sizes first. Subtract allocated space from `total`.\n   - **Pass 2 (Proportional Ratios):** Distribute remaining space among flexible edges according to their `ratio` weights.\n2. **Boundary & Zero Protection Invariants:**\n   - If remaining space is zero or negative, flexible edges must receive `edge.minimum_size` (or 0) without performing division by total ratio weights.\n   - Algorithms must never raise `ZeroDivisionError` on zero-weight column sets; instead, distribute space evenly or fall back to minimum sizes.\n3. **Integer Conservation:**\n   - The sum of resolved column widths must never exceed `total` space allocated by the parent container. Fractional remainders are distributed deterministically across flexible columns.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Prevents crashes in nested or collapsed table views under narrow terminal dimensions.\n- Decouples table column layout logic from split-pane `Layout` mathematics.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":32,"timestamp":1794170976214},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`ADR-0004` outlines a two-pass space resolution algorithm and emphasizes boundary/zero protection invariants for `rich._ratio.py`. This is crucial. It states that flexible edges must receive `edge.minimum_size` (or 0) if remaining space is zero or negative, and that `ZeroDivisionError` should never be raised.\n\nNow I need to examine `KI_rich_null.md` to see the exact implementation details of the ratio solvers, and then `KI_rich_syntax.md` to understand how `Table` utilizes these solvers. I'll start with `KI_rich_null.md`."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_ETiSiapkcyKLhipLKIem","name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","arguments":{"rel_path":".ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_null.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"google/gemini-2.5-flash","usage":{"input":1340,"output":172,"cacheRead":5788,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":7300,"cost":{"input":0.00040199999999999996,"output":0.00043000000000000004,"cacheRead":0.00017364,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00100564,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794170976224,"responseId":"gen-1794170976-TSdvKtSdn1CPlJ3e98wx","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":1156,"thinkingLevel":"off"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_ETiSiapkcyKLhipLKIem","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 -->\n# KI: Rich Core (Internal Utilities & Platform Adaptors)\n\n## Overview\nProvides internal mathematical routines, layout ratio solvers, text wrapping primitives, platform Win32 console structures, and base ABC protocols. It forms the low-level foundation for rendering algorithms.\n\n## Entry Points & Public API\n- `ratio_resolve`: Integer ratio distribution algorithm for flex-like sizing in layouts and tables.\n- `words`: Word wrapping generator yielding split text positions without breaking ANSI tokens.\n- `RichRenderable`: Abstract base class enforcing the `__rich__` rendering protocol.\n- `NullFile`: Dummy writable file descriptor discarding all output.\n\n## Key Components\n| Class / Function | File | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ratio_resolve` | `rich/_ratio.py` | Distributes integer space across items according to ratios and constraints |\n| `words` / `divide_line` | `rich/_wrap.py` | Word and character wrapping algorithms respecting cell widths and unicode boundaries |\n| `NullFile` | `rich/_null_file.py` | In-memory dummy stream implementing file protocol methods as no-ops |\n| `Stack` | `rich/_stack.py` | Lightweight wrapper over list providing stack operations with peak inspection |\n| `LegacyWindowsError` / Win32 structs | `rich/_win32_console.py` | ctypes definitions for Win32 Console API handles, buffers, and coordinates |\n| `RichRenderable` | `rich/abc.py` | Abstract base class verifying presence of `__rich__` magic method |\n| `SPINNERS` | `rich/_spinners.py` | Static catalog of animated spinner frame definitions and refresh intervals |\n\n## Testing & Verification\n- Test commands: `pytest tests/test_ratio.py tests/test_null_file.py tests/test_win32_console.py`\n- Test files: `tests/test_ratio.py`, `tests/test_null_file.py`, `tests/test_win32_console.py`\n\n## Non-obvious Details\n- **Ratio Solvers in `rich/_ratio.py` (ADR-0004)**:\n  - `ratio_resolve(total: int, edges: Sequence[Edge]) -> List[int]` (L14–L85): Solves proportional widths for `Layout` and `Table`. If `total <= 0`, returns `[edge.size or edge.minimum_size or 1 for edge in edges]`. In the loop (L48–L60), `flexible_edges` are resolved using `_Fraction(remaining, sum((edge.ratio or 1) for _, edge in flexible_edges))`. Guard against `sum_ratios <= 0` or `remaining <= 0` to avoid `ZeroDivisionError`.\n  - `ratio_distribute(total: int, ratios: List[int], minimums: Optional[List[int]] = None) -> List[int]` (L107–L145): Distributes integer `total` across `ratios`. Note: if `minimums` is passed, `ratios = [ratio if _min else 0 for ratio, _min in zip(ratios, minimums)]` can zero out all ratios when `minimums` contains zeros, causing `assert total_ratio > 0` (L123) to raise `AssertionError`. When `total <= 0` or `total_ratio <= 0`, it must return `list(minimums)` (if `minimums` is provided) or `[0] * len(ratios)` instead of asserting.\n- **NullFile compatibility**: Some 3rd-party libraries verify `.isatty()` or `.fileno()`; `NullFile` overrides these to gracefully avoid `io.UnsupportedOperation`.\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n- **Direct import of private utilities**: Modules prefixed with `_` (such as `_ratio`, `_wrap`, `_win32_console`) are private and subject to breaking changes across minor versions.\n\n\n## Related KIs\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/cells.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/console.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/color.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]] (via `rich/_loop.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/palette.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/style.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]] (via `rich/text.py`)\n\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":22,"timestamp":1794170977406},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"From `KI_rich_null.md`, I've identified the key functions in `rich/_ratio.py`: `ratio_resolve` and `ratio_distribute`.\n\nSpecifically:\n\n- `ratio_resolve(total: int, edges: Sequence[Edge]) -> List[int]` (L14–L85):\n    - \"If `total <= 0`, returns `[edge.size or edge.minimum_size or 1 for edge in edges]`.\" This is important for preventing zero-width columns.\n    - \"Guard against `sum_ratios <= 0` or `remaining <= 0` to avoid `ZeroDivisionError